WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.610
<v NOVA>Okay. Before we start, I have to
tell you something.

00:00:04.054 --> 00:00:06.214
<v REX>Oh no. Is this the pigeon thing
again?

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.920
<v NOVA>It is not the pigeon thing. Okay.
It's partly the pigeon thing.

00:00:12.926 --> 00:00:18.026
<v NOVA>In nineteen ninety-five, researchers
taught pigeons to tell a painting by Monet

00:00:18.026 --> 00:00:22.666
from one by Picasso. Then they showed them
paintings they had never seen. And the

00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:23.826
pigeons still got it right.

00:00:25.149 --> 00:00:27.489
<v REX>Hang on. Pigeons have better taste in
art than I do?

00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:30.233
<v NOVA>Honestly? Most of us do.

00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:37.413
<v REX>This is Small Wonders, the show about
tiny facts with big stories. I'm Rex.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.550
<v NOVA>And I'm Nova. Today: the surprising
minds of birds.
